# Commander battery module (rev B0) - power path.
#
# Six standard AAA NiMH cells (rechargeable, user-replaceable, sold everywhere; 6S = 7.2 V nominal, 6.0 - 9.4 V) in
# the tray of the chassis model (Group#56: 3 columns x 2 cells, x 57-93, y 77-166).  The cells sit in a plastic
# holder with spring contacts; the holder's harness plugs into J1 (B+ twice, B- twice: 2 A per PH contact).
#
#   cells -> PTC F1 -> P-MOSFET Q1 (reverse polarity: a cell put in the wrong way round cannot hurt anything)
#         -> VBAT -> TPS563201 buck -> 5.0 V on the USB-C port (VBUS) -> mainboard battery port J40
#   VBUS (5 V from the mainboard, when it charges the module) -> MT3608 boost -> D1 -> VBAT -> cells
#
# The buck is ON by default (EN divider = hardware under-voltage cut-off at about 5.8 V = 0.97 V per cell); the
# microcontroller can switch it off (Q2).  It runs in Eco-mode, so it never sinks current: while the mainboard
# pushes 5.05-5.1 V into the port to charge the module, the buck (set to 4.98 V) simply idles, and it takes over
# by itself the moment that voltage goes away - a UPS without a switch-over.  See README.md, "How it works".
#
# Charging is constant-current, controlled by the microcontroller: it measures the cell current (shunt R2 + INA181)
# and trims the boost's set point by a filtered PWM injected into its feedback node.  Hardware ceiling with the PWM
# pin low: 9.4 V (1.56 V per cell); with the pin released (microcontroller off or reset) the boost sits at 4 V,
# below the cells, and EN is pulled low - it cannot charge without the microcontroller.
SHEET batt_power

# Capacitor values carry their voltage rating where the rail goes above 5 V (cells: up to 9.4 V), so JLC's matcher
# cannot pick a 6.3 V part.

# --- cells, protection ---
J1 JST_PH4:CELLS 1=B_POS 2=B_POS 3=B_NEG 4=B_NEG
J2 JST_PH2:NTC_CELLS 1=NTC_EXT 2=GND
F1 PTC1812:2A B_POS B_FUSED
Q1 PMOS_GSD:AO3401A D=B_FUSED S=VBAT G=Q1_G
R1 10K Q1_G GND
TP1 TP VBAT
TP2 TP B_NEG

# --- current sense, low side: 20 mOhm between the cells' minus and ground; INA181A1 (gain 20) with its reference at
#     half supply, so both directions are measured: discharge -> output above REF, charge -> below. +-4 A full scale ---
R2 0R02_1206 GND B_NEG
R3 10R B_NEG ISNS_N
C1 100nF ISNS_N GND
U3 INA181A1 1=ISENSE 2=GND 3=GND 4=ISNS_N 5=ISNS_REF 6=VCC3V3
C2 100nF VCC3V3 GND
R4 100K VCC3V3 ISNS_REF
R5 100K ISNS_REF GND
C3 100nF ISNS_REF GND

# --- charger: boost from VBUS to the cells (MT3608, 2 A switch) ---
#   Vcells(max) = 0.6 V * (1 + R10/R11) + R10 * (0.6 V - Vpwm) / (R12 + R13)
#   = 9.4 V at Vpwm = 0 (ceiling),  5.0 V at Vpwm = 3.3 V (below the cells: no current)
C10 10uF_10V VBUS GND
U4 MT3608 5=VBUS 4=CHG_EN 2=GND 1=CHG_SW 3=CHG_FB
NC U4 6
L1 10uH_2A VBUS CHG_SW
D1 SCHOTTKY:SS34 A=CHG_SW K=VBAT
R10 1M VBAT CHG_FB
R11 75K CHG_FB GND
R12 680K CHG_ISET CHG_FB
R13 68K CHG_PWM CHG_ISET
C13 1uF CHG_ISET GND
R14 100K CHG_EN GND
C11 22uF_16V VBAT GND
C12 22uF_16V VBAT GND

# --- 5 V output: buck from the cells to the port (TPS563201, 3 A) ---
#   VOUT = 0.768 V * (1 + 54.9 / 10) = 4.98 V;  EN: rises past 1.2 V at VBAT = 5.8 V (390k / 100k)
C20 10uF_16V VBAT GND
C21 10uF_16V VBAT GND
U5 TPS563201 3=VBAT 1=GND 2=OUT_SW 4=OUT_FB 5=OUT_EN 6=OUT_BST
C22 100nF OUT_BST OUT_SW
L2 4.7uH_5A OUT_SW VBUS
R20 54.9K VBUS OUT_FB
R21 10K OUT_FB GND
R22 390K VBAT OUT_EN
R23 100K OUT_EN GND
Q2 NMOS_GSD:2N7002 D=OUT_EN S=GND G=OUT_OFF
R24 100K OUT_OFF GND
C23 22uF_10V VBUS GND
C24 22uF_10V VBUS GND
TP3 TP VBUS
TP4 TP GND

# --- 3.3 V for the microcontroller and the sense amplifier: from the cells, or from the port when the cells are flat
#     or out (so the module still enumerates and can report "no battery" / be charged back from empty) ---
U6 BAT54C 1=VBAT 2=VBUS 3=LDO_IN
C30 1uF_16V LDO_IN GND
U7 HT7333 2=LDO_IN 1=GND 3=VCC3V3
C31 4.7uF VCC3V3 GND

# --- measurements for the microcontroller's ADC (reference = VCC3V3) ---
R30 100K VBAT VBAT_ADC
R31 33K VBAT_ADC GND
C32 100nF VBAT_ADC GND
R32 100K VBUS VBUS_ADC
R33 68K VBUS_ADC GND
C33 100nF VBUS_ADC GND
# cell temperature: 10 k B3950 thermistor glued to the middle cell, on J2; a second one on the board edge beside the cells
R34 10K VCC3V3 NTC_EXT
C34 100nF NTC_EXT GND
R35 NTC10K_B3950 NTC_BRD GND
R36 10K VCC3V3 NTC_BRD
